## 2. SLEEVE A: SESSION-OPEN SWEEP AND RECLAIM

This is the primary edge and the highest-trade-count sleeve.

### 2.1 Trading Windows

| Session | Window (UK Time) | Instruments | Reference Range |
|---|---|---|---|
| London | 07:00-11:00 | EURUSD, GBPUSD, XAUUSD | Asian session 00:00-07:00 high and low |
| New York | 13:30-16:00 | XAUUSD, USDJPY | London session 07:00-13:00 high and low |

**Hard exclusions:**
- No entries 21:30-23:30 UK (thin liquidity, spread blowouts)
- Flat every Friday 20:00 UK (weekend gaps respect no stop loss -- SNB 2015, GBP flash 2016, JPY 2022)
- No entries within 30 minutes before or after red-folder news (CPI, NFP, FOMC, rate decisions)
- Hard flatten all positions 15 minutes before and 10 minutes after CPI/NFP/FOMC

### 2.2 The 8-Point Entry Score

Every trade must score at least 7 out of 8 to fire. No exceptions, no override.

| # | Filter | Pass Condition | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Range quality | Range width = 35-75% of its 20-day median width for that instrument | Kills dead tape and exhausted ranges |
| 2 | Higher-timeframe bias | Price on correct side of H1 50-EMA, EMA slope agrees with trade direction. Exception: waived on Asian mean-reversion pairs when H1 ADX below 16 | Trades with the broader trend, not against it |
| 3 | Sweep | Price trades beyond the range extreme by at least 0.15 x ATR(M15, 14), then closes back inside within 3 x M5 candles | Confirms a liquidity sweep, not a genuine breakout |
| 4 | Rejection | The sweep candle has a wick that is at least 60% of its total range | Proves rejection, not continuation |
| 5 | Displacement | The next M5 candle after reclaim has a body at least 60% of its total range and closes beyond the prior candle's midpoint | Confirms institutional displacement in the reversal direction |
| 6 | Spread gate | Live spread is at most 1.5x the 20-day average spread for that symbol | Prevents trading during abnormal cost conditions |
| 7 | Participation | Tick volume on the sweep candle is at least 1.2x the 20-candle average | Confirms real institutional participation, not noise |
| 8 | Clean book | No red-folder news within 30 minutes, no correlated position already open | Prevents news risk and over-concentration |

**Scoring:**
- 8/8: full tier risk (0.24%)
- 7/8: half tier risk (0.12%)
- 6 or below: NO TRADE. No exceptions.

### 2.3 Sweep Depth Validation

The sweep must penetrate beyond the range extreme by between 0.05 and 0.50 x ATR(M15, 14).

- A very small breach (below 0.05 x ATR) is noise, not a sweep
- A very deep breach (above 0.50 x ATR) is more likely a genuine breakout, not a liquidity grab

### 2.4 Entry Order

- Place a limit order at the 50% retracement of the displacement candle's body
- Cancel the order if it remains unfilled after 3 M5 candles (15 minutes)
- Cancel if price reaches +1R before the limit fills
- Cancel if the session entry window closes
- Cancel if a news blackout begins
- Never chase with a market order. If the limit does not fill, the trade is void

### 2.5 Stop Loss

- Long: sweep low minus 0.10 x ATR(M15, 14)
- Short: sweep high plus 0.10 x ATR(M15, 14)
- Reject the trade entirely if the stop distance is below 0.60 x ATR(M15) or above 1.50 x ATR(M15). Too tight means noise will stop you out; too wide means the risk-to-reward is poor

### 2.6 Exit Ladder

All exits are mechanical and automated. No discretion.

| Trigger | Action |
|---|---|
| +1R reached, confirmed by M5 candle close (not wick) | Close 40% of position, move stop to breakeven |
| +2R reached | Close 30% of position |
| Runner (remaining 30%) | Trail at High minus 2.5 x ATR(H1, 14), recalculated hourly |
| 45 minutes elapsed without reaching +1R | Close at market, whatever the P&L |
| Session close | Flat all positions, unless runner is at least +2R with stop already at breakeven |
| Friday 20:00 UK | Flat everything. No exceptions |

**The 45-minute time stop is the single most valuable rule in this entire strategy.** Sweeps displace immediately. If price is still hovering near entry after 45 minutes, the thesis is dead and you are now the liquidity for someone else's sweep. This converts slow-bleed full losers into small scratches and is what lifts net expectancy from marginal to real.

### 2.7 Position Sizing Formula

Position size = (Account Equity x Risk Fraction) / (Stop Distance in pips x Pip Value)

Risk fraction is 0.24% at full tier, 0.12% at half tier, adjusted by the drawdown throttle (see Section 5).

