## 3. SLEEVE B: VOLATILITY-EXPANSION CONTINUATION

This sleeve is deliberately designed to profit on the trending days where Sleeve A gets chopped. It is the sleeve that makes the diversification real.

### 3.1 Trading Windows

| Session | Window (UK Time) | Instruments |
|---|---|---|
| London | 07:00-15:30 | XAUUSD, DAX (GER40) |
| New York | 13:30-19:30 | US30 |

### 3.2 Entry Conditions (All must pass)

1. Daily ATR is in the 60th to 90th percentile of its 20-day range. This sleeve only trades when volatility is genuinely expanding
2. An M15 candle closes beyond the 4-hour range high (for longs) or low (for shorts) with a body that is at least 70% of its total range
3. The breakout candle has tick volume at least 1.3x the 20-candle average
4. Price pulls back to the breakout level within the next 6 M15 candles
5. Enter on a limit order at the breakout level
6. Stop loss: 1.20 x ATR(M15, 14) beyond the breakout candle's extreme

### 3.3 Exit

| Trigger | Action |
|---|---|
| +1.5R | Close 50% of position, move stop to breakeven |
| Remaining 50% | Chandelier trail: highest high since entry minus 3.0 x ATR(H1, 14), recalculated hourly |
| No time stop | This sleeve is supposed to be slow. It rides trends |
| Session close | Flat, unless position is at least +2R with stop at breakeven |
| Friday 20:00 UK | Flat everything |

### 3.4 Scoring

Sleeve B uses a simpler 5-point score. Minimum 4/5 to trade:

| # | Filter | Pass Condition |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | ATR percentile | Daily ATR in 60th-90th percentile of 20-day range |
| 2 | Breakout body | Body at least 70% of candle range |
| 3 | Volume | Tick volume at least 1.3x average |
| 4 | Spread | At most 1.5x average |
| 5 | Clean book | No red-folder news within 30 minutes, no correlated position open |

Score 5/5: full tier (0.24%). Score 4/5: half tier (0.12%). Below 4: no trade.

### 3.5 Expected Trade Count

Approximately 50 trades per month across all instruments and sessions.

