## 5. THE RISK ENGINE: THE SURVIVAL CORE

This is the section that determines whether the account survives 10 years. The entry signal makes the money; the risk engine keeps you alive long enough to collect it.

### 5.1 Per-Trade Risk

- Base risk: 0.24% per trade at full tier (8/8 or 5/5 score)
- Half tier: 0.12% per trade (7/8 or 4/5 score)
- This is approximately 1/10th of full Kelly (correct Kelly is 2.4% for this edge profile, not the 31.3% that some documents claim)

### 5.2 Drawdown Throttle (Hard-Coded, No Override)

Drawdown is measured from the highest closed-equity value, checked before every new order.

| Drawdown from Equity High | Risk per Trade |
|---|---|
| 0 - 2% | 0.24% (full tier) |
| 2 - 4% | 0.12% (half tier) |
| 4 - 6% | 0.06% (quarter tier) |
| Above 6% | Shutdown. No new trades until next month. Mandatory review. |

**Why this specific ladder:** Over 7,200 trades in 10 years (60/month x 120 months), the expected longest losing streak at 45% loss rate is approximately 10 consecutive losses. But real drawdown is not a streak -- it is the worst path of mixed wins and losses, which is 3-4x worse. The correct expected maximum drawdown for this edge profile over 1,000 trades is approximately 15R. At 0.24% risk, that is 3.6% expected max drawdown per sleeve. Across three sleeves with 0.30 correlation, the portfolio expected max drawdown is approximately 6-7%, which fits inside the 8% budget with a small reserve for operational risk.

The throttle ensures that as drawdown grows, risk shrinks automatically. This makes the 10-loss streak that will statistically arrive cost only 1.68% (4 x 0.24% + 4 x 0.12% + 2 x 0.06%), not 2.4%.

### 5.3 Hard Kill Switches

| Trigger | Action |
|---|---|
| Daily loss reaches -1.0% | Stop trading for the rest of the day |
| Weekly loss reaches -2.5% | Stop trading for the rest of the week |
| Monthly drawdown reaches -6% | Stop trading until next month. Mandatory review. |
| 5 consecutive losses on the same instrument and session | Disable that instrument-session combination for 24 hours |
| Rolling 60-trade expectancy of any sleeve drops below 0.08R | That sleeve auto-pauses and alerts. Does not resume until manually reviewed. |
| Live expectancy falls below 50% of backtest after 100 live trades | Full re-validation. No exceptions. |
| Live slippage exceeds 1.5x backtest average | Auto-halve risk on that instrument |
| Spread spike exceeds 2x the 60-minute average | Skip entry, or flatten if already in a trade |
| Latency exceeds 400ms or quote gap exceeds 3 seconds | Flatten everything and halt. Alert. |
| Slippage on last 20 fills exceeds 0.25R average | Halt and alert |

### 5.4 Portfolio-Level Limits

| Limit | Value |
|---|---|
| Max concurrent open positions | 4 total across all sleeves |
| Max concurrent per sleeve | 2 |
| Max total open risk at any moment | 1.0% |
| Max risk per correlated group | 0.24% (EURUSD + GBPUSD same direction = one position) |

### 5.5 Correlation Groups

Treat these as one risk group. Only one position per group at a time:

- USD group: EURUSD, GBPUSD, AUDUSD
- JPY group: USDJPY, GBPJPY, EURJPY
- Commodity group: AUDUSD, USDCAD, XAUUSD (during major US events)
- European cross group: EURGBP, EURCHF

