## 8. DEPLOYMENT GATES (Do Not Skip a Single One)

The robot does not go live until it clears all five gates, in order.

### Gate 1: In-Sample Backtest

- Tick-quality M5 data with real variable spread, 2019-2026
- Must include: March 2020 (COVID crash), 2022 rate shock, 2024-2025 low-vol regime
- Per sleeve, per instrument
- Minimum 200 trades per sleeve
- Gate: expectancy at least 0.18R, profit factor at least 1.30
- A sleeve that fails is not deployed. No "it will work live"

### Gate 2: Walk-Forward

- 6-month train, 2-month test, rolling
- Gate: at least 70% of out-of-sample windows must be profitable
- Out-of-sample expectancy must be at least 60% of in-sample expectancy
- Maximum 4 optimized parameters per sleeve, ever

### Gate 3: Cost Stress Test

- Re-run the backtest with 2x spread and 0.3-pip adverse slippage on every fill
- 10% of profitable limit entries missed (simulates partial fills)
- Occasional stop fills worse by 0.25R
- Random platform interruptions
- Gate: still profit factor at least 1.15. If it fails here, the edge is a spread artifact, not a real edge

### Gate 4: Monte Carlo

- 5,000 trade-order reshuffles at the portfolio level with correlation preserved between sleeves
- Stress each simulation with: spreads multiplied by 1.5, slippage multiplied by 2
- Gate: 95th-percentile maximum drawdown at most 8%
- P(ruin at 15% drawdown) below 1%
- If it fails, cut risk. Never adjust the assumptions to make it pass.

### Gate 5: Forward Demo

- 8 weeks on a live-data demo account
- Same VPS, same broker, same everything
- Full automation, zero manual touches
- Gate: live expectancy within 0.7x of backtest expectancy
- Deviation beyond that means an execution problem. Fix before funding.

### Gate 6: Phased Live Rollout

- Start with one account at 0.12% risk (half the intended 0.24%)
- Add the second account only after 150 profitable live trades
- Add the third account only after another 150 profitable live trades
- Double risk to 0.24% only after live expectancy is confirmed within 70% of backtest

