## 11. THE WHOLE STRATEGY ON ONE CARD

**Architecture:** Three decorrelated sleeves (session-open sweep, volatility-expansion continuation, Asian mean reversion). Returns add linearly; risk adds as square root.

**Sleeve A:** M5 liquidity sweep and reclaim at London and NY opens. EURUSD, GBPUSD, USDJPY, XAUUSD. 8-point score, fire at 7+. Limit at 50% retracement of displacement candle. Stop beyond sweep + 0.10 x ATR. Exit: 40% at +1R, 30% at +2R, 30% trailing. 45-minute hard time stop. ~80 trades/month.

**Sleeve B:** M15 volatility-expansion breakout that holds. XAUUSD, DAX, US30. Daily ATR in 60th-90th percentile. Enter on pullback to breakout level. Stop 1.2 x ATR. Exit: 50% at +1.5R, remainder on Chandelier trail. No time stop. ~50 trades/month.

**Sleeve C:** Asian mean reversion. AUDNZD, EURGBP, EURCHF. ADX below 16, fade 2-sigma Bollinger to mean. Stop 1.0 x ATR. Single target. Hard flat at 06:30 UK. ~70 trades/month.

**Risk:** 0.24% per trade at full tier. Drawdown throttle: 0.24% then 0.12% then 0.06% then shutdown at 6%. Daily -1.0%, weekly -2.5%. Max 1.0% open risk. Correlated pairs count as one position.

**Survival:** 3 accounts at 3 firms. Withdraw 70% of profit monthly. Rolling 30-trade expectancy monitor per sleeve. Annual walk-forward. Max 4 parameters per sleeve. Replace one sleeve every 2-3 years. Shadow account always running.

**Expectation:** 9-11% average month, 13-15% strong month, one or two -3 to -5% months per year. Max drawdown 6-8%. 10-year survival probability 35-40%.

**The two rules that do the heavy lifting:** the 45-minute time stop (turns full losers into scratches) and the drawdown throttle (makes the 10-loss streak survivable). Build those two first and test them in isolation before anything else.

